-- Node: on-hub-start (1 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"info","module":1,"title":"Optic Neuropathy Hub - Sick Check First","body":"**⚠️ 5 DO NOT MISS:**\n1. **Arteritic AION (giant cell arteritis)** — age >50, jaw claudication, scalp tenderness → immediate high-dose steroids.\n2. **Methanol / toxic optic neuropathy** — bilateral loss, high anion-gap acidosis, exposure.\n3. **Pituitary apoplexy / compressive lesion** — sudden loss + headache + ophthalmoplegia.\n4. **Optic neuritis (MS/NMOSD)** — pain on eye movement, RAPD, dyschromatopsia.\n5. **Posterior reversible encephalopathy / occipital stroke** — cortical bilateral pattern, severe HTN.\n\nOpen first:\n- [Hub Steps Summary](#/info/on-hub-steps)\n- [Hub Stop / Pitfalls](#/info/on-hub-stop)\n\n**First 60 seconds (do this every time):**\n- Vitals - HTN crisis? Fever? Tachycardia?\n- Quick neuro - bilateral cortical pattern from PRES / occipital stroke / methanol does NOT stop at the optic nerve\n- **Eye exam every time, both eyes:**\n  - VA (count fingers / hand motion / LP / NLP is fine - do NOT waste time on a Snellen chart in a code stroke)\n  - **RAPD** - the single most useful sign (present = optic nerve / retina, absent = cortical or symmetric pre-chiasmal disease)\n  - **Color desat** (red top of a med bottle works)\n  - Disc exam - pale, swollen, hyperemic, normal\n  - Pupil, **IOP**, lid, extraocular movements\n- If unstable, HTN emergency, methanol suspected, or trauma -> **resus parallel to workup**. Do NOT funnel down \"is this AION\".\n\n**RAPD + central scotoma + color desat = optic nerve until proven otherwise.**\n\nOrganize by time-to-permanent-damage, NOT by mechanism (vascular / inflammatory / compressive). What kills the nerve fastest goes first.","citation":[1,2,3,4],"next":"on-hub-exclusions","summary":"Vitals, neuro, both eyes: VA, RAPD, color, disc, pupil, IOP, lid, EOM. RAPD = optic nerve.","safetyLevel":"critical"}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'on-hub-start' AND tree_id = 'optic-neuropathy-hub';

-- Node: on-hub-gca (1 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"result","module":2,"title":"GCA / Arteritic AION","body":"Open [GCA Deep-Dive](#/tree/gca) when built (placeholder - EB Med Scout queued).\n\n**Next 5 minutes:**\n- **Methylprednisolone 1 g IV NOW** - do NOT wait for biopsy, do NOT wait for ESR/CRP if clinical suspicion is high\n- Send ESR, CRP, CBC (thrombocytosis common), platelets, BMP\n- Temporal artery biopsy scheduled within 1-2 weeks (steroid does NOT invalidate biopsy in the short window)\n- Ophthalmology + rheumatology stat\n- GI prophylaxis PPI + glucose monitoring during high-dose steroid\n\n**Clinical clues:**\n- Age >50 (almost never <50)\n- Jaw claudication (highest LR+)\n- Scalp tenderness, new temporal HA, PMR symptoms (proximal stiffness / shoulder / hip)\n- Constitutional: weight loss, fever, fatigue\n- ESR often >50, CRP almost always up (CRP is more sensitive than ESR)\n- Pale, swollen disc with altitudinal field defect = arteritic AION pattern\n- Amaurosis fugax in the days before frank vision loss is common\n\n**Pitfall:** Do NOT delay steroid for biopsy or test results. Cost of overtreating one false-positive with 3 days of IV steroid is trivial vs cost of a permanent contralateral AION (~30% bilateral rate without treatment).","citation":[5,6,29,30],"recommendation":"Methylpred 1 g IV NOW. ESR/CRP/CBC/plt. Ophtho + rheum stat. Biopsy within 1-2 weeks.","confidence":"definitive","safetyLevel":"critical"}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'on-hub-gca' AND tree_id = 'optic-neuropathy-hub';

-- Node: on-hub-ton (1 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"result","module":2,"title":"Traumatic Optic Neuropathy","body":"Open [Traumatic Optic Neuropathy](#/tree/traumatic-optic-neuropathy) when built (placeholder).\n\n**Next 5 minutes:**\n- CT face + orbits **thin cuts (1 mm bone algorithm)** - thick cuts miss canal fractures\n- Ophthalmology + neurosurgery + oculoplastics stat\n- VA + RAPD + color desat documented at baseline; serial neuro exams\n- Pain control, head of bed up, avoid Valsalva\n- DO NOT give megadose steroid reflexively - CRASH and IOTS data shifted away from routine high-dose methylpred for TBI / TON; institutional decision with consultants\n- Decompression candidates: canalicular fragment + new RAPD + decreasing VA\n\n**Clinical clues:**\n- New RAPD post-trauma is TON until proven otherwise\n- Vision loss may be immediate (direct injury) or delayed (canal hematoma / edema)\n- Often paired with other facial / orbital fractures\n\n**Pitfalls:**\n- Missed canal fracture on thick-cut CT (always ask for thin-cut bone algorithm)\n- Don''t assume the vision loss is \"just orbital edema\" - serial exams matter\n- Do NOT delay neurosurg / oculoplastics consult on the assumption it''s mild","citation":[7,8,31,32],"recommendation":"Thin-cut CT face/orbits. Ophtho + neurosurg + oculoplastics. Serial neuro/VA. Steroid decision is institutional.","confidence":"recommended","safetyLevel":"critical"}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'on-hub-ton' AND tree_id = 'optic-neuropathy-hub';

-- Node: on-hub-methanol (1 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"result","module":2,"title":"Methanol / Toxic Optic Neuropathy","body":"Open [Toxic Alcohols](#/tree/toxic-alcohols).\n\n**Next 5 minutes:**\n- **Fomepizole load 15 mg/kg IV over 30 min**, then 10 mg/kg q12h x 4 doses, then 15 mg/kg q12h until methanol <20 mg/dL AND pH normal\n- Ethanol gtt alternative if fomepizole unavailable: load 0.6-0.8 g/kg IV/PO, maintain level 100-150 mg/dL\n- Bicarb drip for pH <7.30\n- **HD threshold:** methanol level >50, severe acidosis (pH <7.15 unresponsive), end-organ damage (**vision loss IS end-organ**), or renal failure\n- Folinic acid 1 mg/kg IV q4-6h (or folate if folinic unavailable) - accelerates formate metabolism\n- Send: methanol level, ethylene glycol level, ABG, osm gap, lactate, formate, salicylate / acetaminophen co-ingestion screen\n- Poison Control stat\n\n**Clinical clues:**\n- \"Drunk\" patient with vision complaints - always get the gas\n- Bilateral painless vision loss, often progressive over 12-24 h\n- \"Snowfield\" vision, central scotoma, eventually optic disc hyperemia then atrophy\n- High anion gap metabolic acidosis + high osmolar gap\n- Source: bootleg / moonshine, windshield wiper fluid, antifreeze ingestion (suicidal or accidental peds)\n\n**Pitfall:** Fomepizole dose INCREASES AFTER HD - HD removes the drug. Re-dose immediately after the session.","citation":[11,12,33],"recommendation":"Fomepizole load NOW + bicarb + folinic. HD threshold = level >50, pH <7.15, vision loss. Poison Control stat.","confidence":"definitive","safetyLevel":"critical"}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'on-hub-methanol' AND tree_id = 'optic-neuropathy-hub';

-- Node: on-hub-on (1 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"result","module":2,"title":"Optic Neuritis (Demyelinating)","body":"Open [Optic Neuritis](#/tree/optic-neuritis) for full Rx algorithm (subtype work, NMOSD / MOG send-outs, IV methylpred dosing, PLEX criteria, disposition).\n\n**Next 5 minutes:**\n- MRI brain + orbits with fat-sat + gadolinium\n- Send AQP4-IgG and MOG-IgG cell-based assays NOW (before steroid - assay is not affected, but send the bloods first)\n- IV methylprednisolone 1 g IV (1st dose - full course per deep-dive consult)\n- Neuro-ophthalmology consult; neurology consult\n- Rule out infectious mimics first: RPR + treponemal, HIV, CXR if TB risk\n\n**Classic features:**\n- Pain with eye movement (>90% of typical MS-ON)\n- Color desat out of proportion to VA\n- RAPD, central scotoma\n- 2/3 retrobulbar (normal disc), 1/3 papillitis (swollen disc)\n- Often young female, age 20-50\n\n**Pitfalls:**\n- **NEVER oral prednisone alone** - ONTT showed oral pred monotherapy increases recurrence rate\n- Bilateral / severe / no-light-perception / poor recovery -> think NMOSD before MS-ON; pulse longer + add PLEX\n- Always rule out syphilis / TB / HIV before high-dose steroid","citation":[13,14,34],"recommendation":"MRI + AQP4 + MOG + IV methylpred. Never oral pred alone. See [Optic Neuritis](#/tree/optic-neuritis).","confidence":"definitive","safetyLevel":"critical"}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'on-hub-on' AND tree_id = 'optic-neuropathy-hub';

-- Node: on-hub-crao (1 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"result","module":2,"title":"CRAO (Cherry-Red Spot)","body":"Open [CRAO](#/tree/crao) for full hyperacute pathway.\n\n**This is a RETINAL artery occlusion, not technically optic neuropathy** - included in the hub because it presents as sudden painless monocular vision loss and is the most common DDx trap.\n\n**Next 5 minutes:**\n- Treat as a stroke equivalent - **stroke alert / activate stroke team** if within tPA window (some centers now thrombolysing CRAO within 4.5 h)\n- Non-contrast CT head + CTA neck/head (look for carotid embolic source, aortic dissection, ICA stenosis)\n- ESR + CRP - if elevated and age >50, treat as GCA simultaneously (methylpred 1 g IV)\n- ECG + telemetry - look for AFib embolic source\n- Echocardiogram\n- Hyperbaric oxygen if available within window\n- Ophthalmology consult\n\n**Clinical clues:**\n- Sudden painless monocular vision loss (often described as \"curtain coming down\")\n- Cherry-red spot at the fovea (the thinned macula reveals choroidal red against the pale ischemic retina)\n- Pale retina, attenuated arterioles\n- RAPD often profound\n- Embolic risk profile: AFib, carotid stenosis, recent vascular procedure\n\n**Pitfall:** Treating CRAO as \"just an eye problem\" instead of a brain-equivalent stroke. The same patient is at high short-term risk for ipsilateral hemispheric stroke - stroke workup is mandatory.","citation":[16,19,20,29],"recommendation":"Stroke equivalent. Stroke alert, CTA, ESR/CRP for GCA, echo + tele. Tx as per [CRAO](#/tree/crao).","confidence":"definitive","safetyLevel":"critical"}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'on-hub-crao' AND tree_id = 'optic-neuropathy-hub';

-- Node: on-hub-cad (1 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"result","module":2,"title":"Cervical Artery Dissection","body":"Open [Cervical Artery Dissection](#/tree/cervical-artery-dissection).\n\n**Next 5 minutes:**\n- CTA neck + head (or MRA with fat-sat T1 - shows the intramural hematoma)\n- Antiplatelet vs anticoagulation decision per stroke protocol and clot/hemorrhage status\n- Stroke + vascular neurology consult\n- Avoid manipulations of the neck (chiro / massage) and Valsalva activity\n\n**Triad to recognize:**\n- **Horner syndrome** (partial - ptosis + miosis, anhidrosis often absent in carotid dissection because the sweat fibers travel with external carotid)\n- **Neck or face pain** (often unilateral, can be severe and migrainous)\n- **Ischemic event** - amaurosis fugax, monocular vision loss, hemispheric TIA / stroke, or cranial nerve palsy (IX, X, XII)\n\n**Risk factors:** recent neck trauma (often trivial - chiropractic, yoga, sports, MVC whiplash), connective tissue disease (Marfan, Ehlers-Danlos, FMD), recent infection, hypertension.\n\n**Pitfall:** The pain may have started days before the vision loss / TIA - the triad rarely presents all at once. Ask carefully about preceding neck or face pain.","citation":[16,21,22],"recommendation":"CTA neck/head. Antiplatelet/anticoag per stroke protocol. Stroke + vascular consult. Avoid neck manipulation.","confidence":"definitive","safetyLevel":"critical"}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'on-hub-cad' AND tree_id = 'optic-neuropathy-hub';

-- Node: on-hub-orbital (1 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"result","module":2,"title":"Orbital Cellulitis (Compressive Mimicker)","body":"Open [Orbital Cellulitis](#/tree/orbital-cellulitis).\n\n**Next 5 minutes:**\n- IV broad-spectrum antibiotics covering MRSA + anaerobes (vancomycin + ceftriaxone +/- metronidazole; ampicillin-sulbactam if MRSA risk low) - do NOT wait for imaging\n- CT orbits with contrast (look for subperiosteal or orbital abscess, sinusitis source)\n- Ophthalmology + ENT consult; neurosurgery if cavernous sinus involvement suspected\n- VA + EOM + RAPD + pupil + IOP - serial exams\n- Blood cultures, CBC, CRP\n\n**Distinguishes from preseptal cellulitis (eyelid only):**\n- Proptosis (Hertel measurement if available)\n- Painful or restricted EOM\n- Pain with eye movement\n- Decreased VA / color desat\n- RAPD (compressive optic neuropathy)\n- Chemosis\n- Fever / leukocytosis often (but can be absent)\n\n**Pitfalls:**\n- Underdosed empiric antibiotics for orbital cellulitis\n- Missing cavernous sinus thrombosis - look for bilateral findings, CN III/IV/V1/V2/VI involvement\n- Not getting CT contrast (non-con CT misses abscess)","citation":[23,24,35],"recommendation":"Vanc + ceftriaxone IV NOW. CT orbits w/ contrast. Ophtho + ENT. Watch for CST.","confidence":"definitive","safetyLevel":"critical"}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'on-hub-orbital' AND tree_id = 'optic-neuropathy-hub';

-- Node: on-hub-nutritional (1 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"result","module":2,"title":"Nutritional or Hereditary Optic Neuropathy","body":"No deep-dive consult yet (low ED urgency - workup-heavy, outpatient pathway).\n\n**Next 5 minutes / ED workup:**\n- B12, folate, RBC folate, thiamine (B1), copper, ceruloplasmin (Wilson)\n- HIV, RPR + treponemal\n- TSH\n- Heavy metal screen if exposure history (lead, mercury, arsenic)\n- ANA, ENA if autoimmune features\n- If Leber suspected (young male, sequential bilateral, family history): mtDNA testing for 11778, 14484, 3460 (G->A)\n- Pregnancy test if female of reproductive age (B12 deficiency Rx differs)\n- Outpatient neuro-ophthalmology referral - urgent 1-2 weeks\n\n**Clinical clues:**\n- Subacute painless central or cecocentral scotoma\n- Bilateral (often simultaneous or sequential within weeks)\n- ETOH abuse, vegan diet, bariatric surgery history, malabsorption, vitamin A excess (paradoxically)\n- Family history of Leber''s (LHON) - maternal inheritance pattern\n- Slow progressive course (weeks to months)\n\n**Empiric repletion** while workup pends (low risk, high yield):\n- Thiamine 100 mg IM or IV daily x 3 days then PO\n- B12 1000 mcg IM weekly x 4 then monthly\n- Folate 1 mg PO daily\n- Address alcohol use disorder, refer for nutrition\n\n**Pitfall:** Leber''s is often misdiagnosed as MS-ON early - if recovery doesn''t happen at 6 weeks and family history is suggestive, get genetic testing.","citation":[25,26,36],"recommendation":"B12/folate/thiamine/copper/RPR/HIV/TSH. Empiric repletion. Leber genetics if pattern fits. Neuro-ophtho 1-2 weeks.","confidence":"recommended","safetyLevel":"warning"}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'on-hub-nutritional' AND tree_id = 'optic-neuropathy-hub';

-- Node: on-hub-rescue (1 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"info","module":3,"title":"Rescue / Initial Bundle + Reassess","body":"**Default bundle when no single cause declares itself:**\n\n**Bedside:**\n- VA both eyes (CF / HM / LP / NLP is fine)\n- Confirm RAPD\n- Ishihara 1-2 plates (color desat documentation)\n- Disc photo via fundus camera if available; dilated exam by ophtho otherwise\n- IOP both eyes - rule out AACG mimicker (AACG hurts, IOP >40, mid-dilated fixed pupil; route to [AACG](#/tree/aacg))\n- Formal Humphrey field if available, otherwise confrontation\n- POCUS optic nerve sheath if elevated ICP suspected (adult >5 mm, peds >4.5 mm at 3 mm posterior to globe)\n\n**Labs:**\n- ESR, CRP, CBC, BMP, glucose\n- B12, folate, RPR, HIV (demographic-driven)\n- Pregnancy if applicable\n\n**Imaging:**\n- See Module 4 - MRI brain + orbits with fat-sat + gad is the default for most \"unsure\" presentations\n\n**Universal:**\n- Ophthalmology consult ALWAYS for new optic neuropathy\n- If ANY suspicion of GCA (age >50, scalp / jaw / PMR / new HA, ESR or CRP up): **empiric methylpred 1 g IV NOW** - do not wait for biopsy or labs\n\n**Reassess at 60 min:**\n- VA stable or improving -> continue workup, ophtho disposition\n- VA dropping or RAPD worsening -> STOP, back to Module 2 (something time-critical was missed), re-image, re-consult\n- New neuro finding -> back to Module 2 (PRES / pituitary / methanol / stroke)","citation":[1,2,3,4,6,29],"next":"on-hub-reassess","summary":"Bedside: VA, RAPD, color, disc, IOP, fields, ONS US. Labs: ESR/CRP/CBC + targeted. Always ophtho. Empiric pulse if GCA.","safetyLevel":"critical"}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'on-hub-rescue' AND tree_id = 'optic-neuropathy-hub';

-- Node: on-hub-reassess (1 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"question","module":3,"title":"Reassess at 60 min","body":"Recheck VA, RAPD, neuro exam after the initial bundle.","citation":[1,4],"options":[{"label":"VA dropping, RAPD worsening, or new neuro finding","description":"Back to exclusions","next":"on-hub-exclusions","urgency":"critical"},{"label":"Stable, unsorted, awaiting imaging / labs","description":"Imaging decision","next":"on-hub-imaging"},{"label":"Stable, cause clear, ophtho on board","description":"Disposition","next":"on-hub-dispo"}],"summary":"Worsening -> exclusions. Stable + unsorted -> imaging. Stable + clear -> disposition."}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'on-hub-reassess' AND tree_id = 'optic-neuropathy-hub';

-- Node: on-hub-imaging (1 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"info","module":4,"title":"Imaging Decision","body":"**MRI brain + orbits WITH gadolinium + fat-saturation orbit sequences** - first-line for:\n- Demyelinating ON\n- Compressive lesions (tumor, mass, sellar / parasellar)\n- Pituitary apoplexy (add dedicated sella cuts)\n- CVST suspicion (add MRV)\n- PRES\n\n**CT face + orbits thin-cut (1 mm bone algorithm)** - first-line for:\n- Trauma -> [TON](#/tree/traumatic-optic-neuropathy)\n- Sinusitis with compression\n- Orbital cellulitis -> [Orbital Cellulitis](#/tree/orbital-cellulitis)\n\n**MRV** - mandatory in:\n- IIH workup (CVST mimics IIH and kills) -> [IIH](#/tree/iih)\n- Pituitary apoplexy with concern for sinus thrombosis\n\n**CTA neck + head** - mandatory when:\n- Horner + pain + monocular vision loss -> [Cervical Artery Dissection](#/tree/cervical-artery-dissection)\n- CRAO (look for embolic source) -> [CRAO](#/tree/crao)\n- Suspected occipital stroke or hemispheric event\n\n**POCUS optic nerve sheath** - bedside ICP screen:\n- Adult cutoff >5 mm at 3 mm posterior to globe\n- Peds >4.5 mm\n- Infant <1 yr >4.0 mm\n- Sensitivity ~90%, specificity ~85% for ICP >20 cm H2O\n- Adjunct only - not a substitute for fundoscopy or LP\n\n**NO imaging for:**\n- Straightforward stable subacute nutritional or drug-induced presentations with confirmed ophtho follow-up within 1 week\n\n**Imaging-not-imaging recall checklist:**\n- Age >50 with new vision loss -> image AND treat as GCA until proven otherwise\n- Any HA + vision change -> MRI / MRV before discharge\n- Trauma -> CT thin-cut, always\n- Bilateral disc swelling -> MRI + MRV, always","citation":[1,4,5,17,19],"next":"on-hub-dispo","summary":"MRI brain+orbits w/gad+fat-sat default. CT trauma/sinus. MRV for IIH/CVST. CTA for Horner/CRAO. ONS US bedside.","safetyLevel":"critical"}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'on-hub-imaging' AND tree_id = 'optic-neuropathy-hub';

-- Node: on-hub-dispo (1 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"question","module":5,"title":"Disposition","body":"Disposition is cause-specific. Defer to the deep-dive consult''s admit criteria once the phenotype is committed.","citation":[1,6,29],"options":[{"label":"GCA on IV steroids / TON / pit apoplexy / methanol on HD or fomepizole / severe ON / PRES / cortical / cellulitis","description":"Admit per cause","next":"on-hub-dispo-admit","urgency":"critical"},{"label":"Equivocal awaiting biopsy / single-dose pulse given outpatient infusion arranged","description":"Observe","next":"on-hub-dispo-observe"},{"label":"Stable subacute, ophtho confirmed within 1 week, drug stopped, nutritional repletion started","description":"Discharge with follow-up","next":"on-hub-dispo-discharge"}],"summary":"Admit for life/sight-threat; observe for equivocal; discharge with confirmed 1-week ophtho follow-up."}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'on-hub-dispo' AND tree_id = 'optic-neuropathy-hub';

-- Node: on-hub-dispo-admit (1 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"result","module":5,"title":"Admit","body":"Admit for:\n- GCA on IV steroids pending biopsy (~24-72 h depending on pulse + bridge plan)\n- TON for serial neuro / VA checks (24-72 h minimum)\n- Pituitary apoplexy - ICU or neurosurg floor\n- Methanol on HD or fomepizole drip - ICU\n- Severe / NMOSD / MOG optic neuritis during pulse and PLEX coordination\n- PRES, malignant HTN, occipital stroke - admit per home consult\n- Orbital cellulitis on IV antibiotics\n- IIH with severe papilledema or VA dropping despite acetazolamide\n- Cervical artery dissection per stroke service\n- Any unstable patient\n\n**Inpatient orders (universal):**\n- Continue cause-specific therapy (steroid pulse, antibiotics, fomepizole, antihypertensive drip)\n- Daily ophtho or neuro-ophtho exam\n- Glucose / BP / GI prophylaxis during high-dose steroid\n- DVT prophylaxis per usual\n- Suicide screen if vision loss is permanent / severe\n- Specialty consult: ophtho + cause-specific (rheum / neuro / endo / NSG / ID)\n- Pending workup tracker: biopsy, AQP4 / MOG, cultures, MRI report finalized, CSF if obtained","citation":[1,6,17,29],"recommendation":"Admit for life- or sight-threat. Continue cause-specific Rx. Specialty consults + daily exams.","confidence":"definitive","safetyLevel":"critical"}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'on-hub-dispo-admit' AND tree_id = 'optic-neuropathy-hub';

-- Node: on-hub-dispo-observe (1 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"result","module":5,"title":"Observation","body":"Observation appropriate for:\n- Equivocal GCA awaiting biopsy results with steroids on board, stable VA\n- Single-dose IV methylpred given, outpatient infusion arranged, awaiting ride / transport\n- IIH / papilledema awaiting LP opening pressure / MRV results\n- Partial workup pending; follow-up not yet confirmed by phone\n\n**Observation orders:**\n- Continue cause-specific therapy\n- Serial VA / neuro exams\n- Glucose, BP, GI prophylaxis if on steroid\n- Confirm follow-up appointment by phone before discharge (do NOT just hand out a phone number)\n- Specialty consult before disposition\n\n**Convert to admit if:** worsening VA, new neuro finding, severe side effect of therapy, social barrier preventing safe discharge, or workup result that upgrades acuity (positive AQP4-IgG, severe sinusitis on CT, etc.).","citation":[1,6,29],"recommendation":"Observe for equivocal / pending workup / awaiting outpatient logistics. Confirm follow-up before discharge.","confidence":"recommended","safetyLevel":"warning"}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'on-hub-dispo-observe' AND tree_id = 'optic-neuropathy-hub';

-- Node: on-hub-dispo-discharge (1 field(s) changed)
UPDATE decision_nodes SET data = '{"type":"result","module":5,"title":"Discharge","body":"**Discharge criteria:**\n- Stable subacute / chronic presentation with confirmed neuro-ophthalmology follow-up within 1 week\n- Drug-induced with offender stopped (or coordinated stop plan) + outpatient plan\n- Stable nutritional cause with B12 / folate / thiamine replacement started + follow-up\n- Typical MS-ON discharged after first IV methylpred dose with confirmed outpatient infusion\n\n**Universal discharge checklist:**\n- VA documented at discharge (compare to arrival)\n- Pain controlled\n- Orthostatic vitals normal (high-dose steroid can drop BP and unmask adrenal issues)\n- No new neuro findings on recheck\n- Written return precautions: any new vision change, contralateral eye involvement, headache, weakness, numbness, slurred speech -> return immediately\n- Follow-up arranged AND confirmed by phone (call the office, do not just hand a phone number)\n- Suicide screen if any vision loss is permanent (acute vision loss has elevated SI rates)\n- Pregnancy plan documented if applicable\n- Patient understands the diagnosis hypothesis and the plan\n\n**Return precautions (universal):**\n- Worsening or new vision loss in either eye\n- Severe headache, fever, neck stiffness\n- New weakness, numbness, gait change, bladder / bowel\n- Inability to tolerate oral steroid taper\n- Severe steroid side effects (mood change, GI bleed signs, glucose crisis)","citation":[1,6,29],"recommendation":"Discharge only with confirmed 1-week ophtho follow-up, return precautions understood, suicide screen documented.","confidence":"recommended","safetyLevel":"warning"}'::jsonb
WHERE id = 'on-hub-dispo-discharge' AND tree_id = 'optic-neuropathy-hub';

